.TH CANOPA-NOTIFY 1 "September 2026" "Canopa Notify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
canopa-notify \- Wayland desktop notifications and local notification history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B canopa-notify daemon --service --socket
.I PATH
.RB [ --database " PATH"]
.RB [ --config " PATH" | --canopa-config " PATH"]
.br
.B canopa-notify daemon --headless --socket
.I PATH
.RB [ --database " PATH"]
.RB [ --dev-bus-name " NAME"]
.br
.B canopa-notify ctl --socket
.I PATH COMMAND
.br
.B canopa-notify panel-provider --socket
.I PATH
.SH DESCRIPTION
Canopa Notify owns org.freedesktop.Notifications on the session bus in service
mode. It displays banners without taking keyboard focus and provides a
Notification Center through a compatible Niribar host. Service mode requires
Wayland and the wlr layer-shell protocol. Headless mode is intended for tests and
development; a development bus name must be requested explicitly.
.PP
Startup refuses competing ownership before recovering the database. Existing
sender IDs and actions become invalid after restart. Retained notifications keep
their attention state; transient notifications do not survive restart.
.SH CONFIGURATION CHECKING
.B canopa-notify check-config
validates the notification namespace without starting a service. Options include
--config PATH (legacy), --canopa-config PATH (shared), --defaults, and --show-source
(local diagnostic detail). The canopa config check command checks both components.
.SH CONTROL COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--json]
Report daemon, configuration, rendering, sender-publication and link-opening health.
.TP
.B active [--json]
List current sender lifecycles. Expired retained attention is available in the Center.
.TP
.B dnd [status|on|off|toggle]
Read or persist Do Not Disturb. Changes affect subsequent notification requests.
.TP
.B reload [PATH]
Validate and install a configuration candidate. Failure retains the last good
configuration. PATH selects legacy flat syntax. Without PATH, repeat the last
committed selection, including discovery when started without an explicit file.
.TP
.B reload-canopa PATH
Select and install the notifications namespace of an explicit shared Canopa file.
.TP
.B clear
Dismiss active notifications, including runtime-only transient items.
.TP
.B delete-history
Explicitly remove inactive retained history, including unacknowledged items.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/canopa/config.kdl
Shared KDL envelope with schema-version 1 and optional shell/notifications blocks.
The fallback directory is ~/.config. Missing namespaces use embedded defaults.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/canopa-notify/config.kdl
Legacy flat rules, sound settings and icon theme/scale; used only when the shared file is absent. The fallback is
~/.config/canopa-notify/config.kdl. See the distributed examples/config.kdl.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/canopa-notify/history.db
Durable history, attention, DND and user rules. The fallback is
~/.local/state/canopa-notify/history.db. Back up while the daemon is stopped.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/canopa-notify/control.sock
Private control socket used by the supplied systemd user unit. CLI invocations
always specify the socket explicitly. The runtime directory is not durable storage.
.SH OPERATION
The supplied user unit installs the binary at ~/.local/bin/canopa-notify and is
bound to graphical-session.target. Import WAYLAND_DISPLAY and XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
into the systemd user manager before starting the unit. Stop another notification
daemon first. Consult journalctl --user -u canopa-notify.service for diagnostics.
.PP
Database migrations are forward only. Restore a pre-upgrade backup before running
an older binary that cannot read the new schema. An unavailable renderer is
reported in status; restart the daemon to restore banners.
.PP
Body links accept HTTP and HTTPS and open through the desktop OpenURI portal.
Unsupported targets remain visible text. Opening a link does not invoke the
sender's default action or dismiss the notification.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates invalid arguments, startup failure,
rejected control input or an unsuccessful exchange. A failed exchange after
transmission can have an unknown command outcome; inspect state before retrying.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify-send (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
